IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `ucta-nouns`
IMPORT `ucta-logic`

-- Unfair Contract Terms Act 1977 (Singapore), 2020 Revised Edition, informal consolidation.
-- LAYER 1, MODULE 4: PART 3 (Miscellaneous), sections 26 to 30.
-- Part 2 (sections 15 to 25, Scotland) is shown in the text only as a bracketed note; it has no module.
--
-- READING A RESULT (see NOTES.md, "Reading a result: FALSE and NOTHING").
--   * JUST FALSE : the text says no in its own words ("do not apply", "is not precluded", "only if",
--                  a definition that "means", or a positive effect whose "if" or "where" fails);
--   * JUST TRUE  : the text says yes in its own words;
--   * NOTHING    : not covered: silent, list not closed, includes, undefined term, points outside
--                  the text (the Minister's order, the Civil Law Act 1909), or limited by its own wording.
-- A caller must never turn NOTHING into FALSE.

§ `Part 3 - International supply contracts (s 26)`

-- src:437 | (3) Subject to subsection (4), that description of contract is one
-- src:438 | whose characteristics are the following:
-- src:440 | (a) either it is a contract of sale of goods or it is one under or in
-- src:441 | pursuance of which the possession or ownership of goods
-- src:442 | passes; and
-- src:444 | (b) it is made by parties whose places of business (or, if they
-- src:445 | have none, habitual residences) are in the territories of
-- src:446 | different States.
-- src:448 | (4) A contract falls within subsection (3) only if either —
-- src:450 | (a) the goods in question are, at the time of the conclusion of
-- src:451 | the contract, in the course of carriage, or will be carried,
-- src:452 | from the territory of one State to the territory of another;
-- src:454 | (b) the acts constituting the offer and acceptance have been
-- src:455 | done in the territories of different States; or
-- src:457 | (c) the contract provides for the goods to be delivered to the
-- src:458 | territory of a State other than that within whose territory
-- src:459 | those acts were done.
@ref s 26(3) and (4) (src:437-459)
GIVEN kind IS A `Kind of contract`
      part3 IS A `Part 3 facts`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 26(3) and (4) the contract is an international supply contract` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF kind EQUALS `Another kind of contract`
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "that description of contract is one whose characteristics are the following: (a) either it is a contract of sale of goods or it is one under or in pursuance of which the possession or ownership of goods passes" -- a definition by conditions; this contract is neither
        THEN JUST FALSE
        IF NOT part3's `the parties have places of business (or, if none, habitual residences) in the territories of different States`
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "(b) it is made by parties whose places of business (or, if they have none, habitual residences) are in the territories of different States" -- a definition by conditions; limb (b) is not met
        THEN JUST FALSE
        IF NOT (   part3's `the goods are, when the contract is concluded, in the course of carriage or will be carried from one State to another`
                OR part3's `the acts constituting the offer and acceptance were done in the territories of different States`
                OR part3's `the contract provides for delivery to a State other than the one in which those acts were done`)
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "A contract falls within subsection (3) only if either (a) ...; (b) ...; or (c) ..." -- none of (a), (b) or (c) is met
        THEN JUST FALSE
        -- TRUE-kind (the text says yes in its own words): subsection (3)(a) and (b) are met and one of subsection (4)(a), (b) or (c) is met
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- src:429 | 26.—(1) The limits imposed by this Act on the extent to which a
-- src:430 | person may exclude or restrict liability by reference to a contract term
-- src:431 | do not apply to liability arising under such a contract as is described in
-- src:432 | subsection (3).
@ref s 26(1) (src:429-432)
GIVEN kind IS A `Kind of contract`
      part3 IS A `Part 3 facts`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 26(1) the limits imposed by this Act on excluding or restricting liability apply to liability under the contract` MEANS
    IF `s 26(3) and (4) the contract is an international supply contract` kind part3 EQUALS JUST TRUE
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The limits imposed by this Act ... do not apply to liability arising under such a contract as is described in subsection (3)"
    THEN JUST FALSE
    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): subsection (1) speaks only of "such a contract as is described in subsection (3)"; for any other contract it says nothing (a scope limit with no "only")
    ELSE NOTHING

-- src:434 | (2) The terms of such a contract are not subject to any requirement
-- src:435 | of reasonableness under section 3 or 4.
@ref s 26(2) (src:434-435)
GIVEN kind IS A `Kind of contract`
      part3 IS A `Part 3 facts`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 26(2) the terms of the contract are subject to a requirement of reasonableness under section 3 or 4` MEANS
    IF `s 26(3) and (4) the contract is an international supply contract` kind part3 EQUALS JUST TRUE
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The terms of such a contract are not subject to any requirement of reasonableness under section 3 or 4"
    THEN JUST FALSE
    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): subsection (2) speaks only of "such a contract"
    ELSE NOTHING

§ `Part 3 - Choice of law clauses (s 27)`

-- src:464 | 27.—(1) Where the proper law of a contract is the law of Singapore
-- src:465 | only by choice of the parties (and apart from that choice would be the
-- src:466 | law of some country outside Singapore) sections 2 to 7 do not operate
-- src:467 | as part of the proper law.
@ref s 27(1) (src:464-467)
GIVEN part3 IS A `Part 3 facts`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 27(1) sections 2 to 7 operate as part of the proper law` MEANS
    IF part3's `the proper law is the law of Singapore only by choice of the parties`
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where the proper law of a contract is the law of Singapore only by choice of the parties (and apart from that choice would be the law of some country outside Singapore) sections 2 to 7 do not operate as part of the proper law"
    THEN JUST FALSE
    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): subsection (1) is a negative statement conditioned by "Where"; if the proper law is Singapore law for another reason it does not say that sections 2 to 7 operate (that would be a yes the text does not give); its own words, "do not operate", are `s 27(1) sections 2 to 7 do not operate as part of the proper law`, which answers JUST FALSE outside the "Where" (fork F6, site s 27(1))
    ELSE NOTHING

-- src:464 | 27.—(1) Where the proper law of a contract is the law of Singapore
-- src:465 | only by choice of the parties (and apart from that choice would be the
-- src:466 | law of some country outside Singapore) sections 2 to 7 do not operate
-- src:467 | as part of the proper law.
@ref s 27(1), the provision applies (src:464-467)
GIVEN part3 IS A `Part 3 facts`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 27(1) sections 2 to 7 do not operate as part of the proper law` MEANS
    IF part3's `the proper law is the law of Singapore only by choice of the parties`
    -- TRUE-kind (the text says yes in its own words): "Where the proper law of a contract is the law of Singapore only by choice of the parties (and apart from that choice would be the law of some country outside Singapore) sections 2 to 7 do not operate as part of the proper law"
    THEN JUST TRUE
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words; marginal reading for a lawyer, a failed "Where" on a negative statement is the text's no, ruling of 2026-11-05 (b)): the proper law is the law of Singapore for another reason (or is not Singapore law), so the subsection does not switch sections 2 to 7 off; it does not say they operate either (see `s 27(1) sections 2 to 7 operate as part of the proper law`)
    ELSE JUST FALSE

-- src:469 | (2) This Act has effect notwithstanding any contract term which
-- src:470 | applies or purports to apply the law of some country outside
-- src:471 | Singapore, where (either or both) —
-- src:473 | (a) the term appears to the court, or arbitrator or arbiter to have
-- src:474 | been imposed wholly or mainly for the purpose of enabling
-- src:475 | the party imposing it to evade the operation of this Act; or
-- src:477 | (b) in the making of the contract one of the parties dealt as
-- src:478 | consumer, and he was then habitually resident in
-- src:479 | Singapore, and the essential steps necessary for the
-- src:480 | making of the contract were taken there, whether by him
-- src:481 | or by others on his behalf.
@ref s 27(2) (src:469-481)
GIVEN `the contract has a term which applies or purports to apply the law of a country outside Singapore` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the term appears to the court, arbitrator or arbiter to have been imposed wholly or mainly to enable the party imposing it to evade this Act` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `in the making of the contract one of the parties dealt as consumer` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `that party was then habitually resident in Singapore` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the essential steps necessary for the making of the contract were taken in Singapore` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 27(2) this Act has effect notwithstanding the term applying the law of a country outside Singapore` MEANS
    IF NOT `the contract has a term which applies or purports to apply the law of a country outside Singapore`
    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): subsection (2) speaks of "any contract term which applies or purports to apply the law of some country outside Singapore"; with no such term it says nothing
    THEN NOTHING
    ELSE CONSIDER `limb a` `or else` `limb b`
        -- TRUE-kind (the text says yes in its own words): "This Act has effect notwithstanding any contract term which applies or purports to apply the law of some country outside Singapore, where (either or both) (a) ...; or (b) ..."
        WHEN JUST TRUE THEN JUST TRUE
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): the "where" fails -- neither (a) nor (b) is met (ruling of 2026-11-05: a failed "where" on a positive effect answers JUST FALSE)
        WHEN JUST FALSE THEN JUST FALSE
        -- NOTHING-kind (undefined term): limb (a) turns on what "appears to the court, or arbitrator or arbiter", a judgment the Act leaves to them, or limb (b) on whether a party dealt as consumer, which is not given
        WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
    WHERE
        `limb a` MEANS `the term appears to the court, arbitrator or arbiter to have been imposed wholly or mainly to enable the party imposing it to evade this Act`
        `limb b` MEANS (`consumer` `and also` `resident`) `and also` `steps`
        `consumer` MEANS `in the making of the contract one of the parties dealt as consumer`
        `resident` MEANS `known to be` `that party was then habitually resident in Singapore`
        `steps` MEANS `known to be` `the essential steps necessary for the making of the contract were taken in Singapore`

§ `Part 3 - Provision for sea carriage of passengers (s 28)`

-- src:485 | 28.—(1) This section applies to a contract for carriage by sea of a
-- src:486 | passenger or of a passenger and his luggage.
@ref s 28(1) (src:485-486)
GIVEN part3 IS A `Part 3 facts`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 28(1) section 28 applies to the contract` MEANS
    IF part3's `the contract is for the carriage by sea of a passenger, or of a passenger and luggage`
    -- TRUE-kind (the text says yes in its own words): "This section applies to a contract for carriage by sea of a passenger or of a passenger and his luggage"
    THEN JUST TRUE
    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the section is about "a contract for carriage by sea of a passenger" (a scope limit with no "only")
    ELSE NOTHING

-- src:488 | (2) A person is not precluded by this Act from excluding or
-- src:489 | restricting liability for loss or damage in such circumstances and to
-- src:490 | such extent as may be prescribed by order made by the Minister by
-- src:491 | reference to a term of the contract so prescribed.
@ref s 28(2) (src:488-491)
GIVEN part3 IS A `Part 3 facts`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 28(2) this Act precludes the person from excluding or restricting liability for loss or damage` MEANS
    IF NOT part3's `the contract is for the carriage by sea of a passenger, or of a passenger and luggage`
    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): section 28 applies to "a contract for carriage by sea of a passenger or of a passenger and his luggage" (subsection (1))
    THEN NOTHING
    ELSE CONSIDER part3's `the Minister's order prescribes this exclusion in these circumstances, to this extent, by this term`
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "A person is not precluded by this Act from excluding or restricting liability for loss or damage in such circumstances and to such extent as may be prescribed by order made by the Minister by reference to a term of the contract so prescribed" -- the order prescribes this
        WHEN JUST TRUE THEN JUST FALSE
        -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the order does not prescribe this circumstance, extent and term, so the subsection does not lift the Act's limits
        WHEN JUST FALSE THEN NOTHING
        -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): the Minister's order is not among the sources
        WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING

§ `Part 3 - Saving for other relevant legislation (s 29)`

-- src:516 | (3) In this section —
-- src:518 | “competent authority” means any court, arbitrator or arbiter,
-- src:519 | Government department or public authority;
-- src:521 | “enactment” means any legislation (including subsidiary
-- src:522 | legislation) of Singapore and any instrument having effect
-- src:523 | by virtue of such legislation;
-- src:525 | “statutory” means conferred by an enactment.
@ref s 29(3), "enactment" (src:516-525)
GIVEN instrument IS A `Kind of instrument`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 29(3) the instrument is an enactment` MEANS
    CONSIDER instrument
    -- TRUE-kind (the text says yes in its own words): "enactment means any legislation (including subsidiary legislation) of Singapore"
    WHEN `Legislation of Singapore` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `Subsidiary legislation of Singapore` THEN JUST TRUE
    -- TRUE-kind (the text says yes in its own words): "and any instrument having effect by virtue of such legislation"
    WHEN `An instrument having effect by virtue of legislation of Singapore` THEN JUST TRUE
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "enactment means ..." -- a definition that "means"; anything else is not an enactment
    WHEN `Something else` THEN JUST FALSE

GIVEN body IS A `Kind of body`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 29(3) the body is a competent authority` MEANS
    CONSIDER body
    -- TRUE-kind (the text says yes in its own words): "competent authority means any court, arbitrator or arbiter, Government department or public authority"
    WHEN `A court` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `An arbitrator or arbiter` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `A Government department` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `A public authority` THEN JUST TRUE
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "competent authority means ..." -- a definition that "means"; any other body is not a competent authority
    WHEN `Another body` THEN JUST FALSE

GIVEN `conferred by` IS A `Kind of instrument`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 29(3) the jurisdiction or function is statutory` MEANS
    -- "statutory means conferred by an enactment": a jurisdiction or function is statutory exactly when the instrument that confers it is an enactment
    `s 29(3) the instrument is an enactment` `conferred by`

-- src:495 | 29.—(1) Nothing in this Act removes or restricts the effect of, or
-- src:496 | prevents reliance upon, any contractual provision which —
-- src:498 | (a) is authorised or required by the express terms or necessary
-- src:499 | implication of an enactment; or
-- src:501 | (b) being made with a view to compliance with an
-- src:502 | international agreement to which Singapore is a party,
-- src:503 | does not operate more restrictively than is contemplated by
-- src:504 | the agreement.
@ref s 29(1) (src:495-504)
GIVEN part3 IS A `Part 3 facts`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 29(1) this Act removes or restricts the effect of, or prevents reliance upon, the contractual provision` MEANS
    IF `limb a` `or else` `limb b` EQUALS JUST TRUE
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Nothing in this Act removes or restricts the effect of, or prevents reliance upon, any contractual provision which (a) ... or (b) ..."
    THEN JUST FALSE
    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the subsection speaks only of a provision "which" is authorised or required by an enactment, or made to comply with an international agreement and not more restrictive than it contemplates (a scope limit with no "only")
    ELSE NOTHING
    WHERE
        `limb a` MEANS `authorised` `and also` (`s 29(3) the instrument is an enactment` (part3's `that instrument`))
        `authorised` MEANS `known to be` (part3's `the provision is authorised or required by the express terms or necessary implication of an instrument`)
        `limb b` MEANS `compliance` `and also` `not more restrictive`
        `compliance` MEANS `known to be` (part3's `the provision was made with a view to compliance with an international agreement to which Singapore is a party`)
        `not more restrictive` MEANS `known to be` (part3's `the provision does not operate more restrictively than the agreement contemplates`)

-- src:509 | (2) A contract term is to be taken for the purposes of Part 1 as
-- src:510 | satisfying the requirement of reasonableness if it is incorporated or
-- src:511 | approved by, or incorporated pursuant to a decision or ruling of, a
-- src:512 | competent authority acting in the exercise of any statutory
-- src:513 | jurisdiction or function and is not a term in a contract to which the
-- src:514 | competent authority is itself a party.
@ref s 29(2) (src:509-514)
GIVEN `it is incorporated or approved by, or incorporated pursuant to a decision or ruling of, the body` IS A BOOLEAN
      body IS A `Kind of body`
      `the body is acting in the exercise of a jurisdiction or function conferred by` IS A `Kind of instrument`
      `the contract is one to which the competent authority is itself a party` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 29(2) the contract term is taken as satisfying the requirement of reasonableness` MEANS
    IF all
    -- TRUE-kind (the text says yes in its own words): "A contract term is to be taken for the purposes of Part 1 as satisfying the requirement of reasonableness if it is incorporated or approved by, or incorporated pursuant to a decision or ruling of, a competent authority acting in the exercise of any statutory jurisdiction or function and is not a term in a contract to which the competent authority is itself a party"
    THEN JUST TRUE
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): the "if" is not met (marginal reading for a lawyer: a failed "if" is taken as the text's no for the deeming; the term may still satisfy the requirement under section 11)
    ELSE JUST FALSE
    WHERE
        all MEANS
                `it is incorporated or approved by, or incorporated pursuant to a decision or ruling of, the body`
            AND `s 29(3) the body is a competent authority` body EQUALS JUST TRUE
            AND `s 29(3) the jurisdiction or function is statutory` `the body is acting in the exercise of a jurisdiction or function conferred by` EQUALS JUST TRUE
            AND NOT `the contract is one to which the competent authority is itself a party`

§ `Part 3 - Short title and transitional (s 30)`

-- s 30(1): "This Act may be cited as the Unfair Contract Terms Act 1977." Machinery (short title); not encoded.

-- src:532 | (2) Nothing in this Act applies in relation to a contract made or
-- src:533 | liability for loss or damage suffered before 12 November 1993 except
-- src:534 | in so far as it was applicable by virtue of section 5 of the Civil Law
-- src:535 | Act 1909 in force before that date.
@ref s 30(2) (src:532-535)
GIVEN part3 IS A `Part 3 facts`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 30(2) this Act applies in relation to the contract or the liability for loss or damage` MEANS
    IF NOT before
    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "before 12 November 1993" -- both the contract and the loss fall on or after that day, and subsection (2) says nothing about them (a negative statement outside its period)
    THEN NOTHING
    ELSE CONSIDER part3's `it was applicable by virtue of section 5 of the Civil Law Act 1909 in force before that date`
        -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "except in so far as it was applicable by virtue of section 5 of the Civil Law Act 1909" -- the exception is met, so the bar does not apply and the subsection grants nothing (QA)
        WHEN JUST TRUE THEN NOTHING
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Nothing in this Act applies in relation to a contract made or liability for loss or damage suffered before 12 November 1993"
        WHEN JUST FALSE THEN JUST FALSE
        -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): whether section 5 of the Civil Law Act 1909 made the Act applicable is not among the sources
        WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
    WHERE
        `the day` MEANS Date 12 11 1993
        before MEANS
                part3's `the date the contract was made` LESS THAN `the day`
             OR part3's `the date the loss or damage was suffered` LESS THAN `the day`

§ `Part 3 - Part 3 and Part 1: whether an exception takes the case out (s 1(2))`

-- s 1(2): "This Part is subject to Part 3".  This function gathers, by hand, the Part 3 provisions that
-- take a case out of sections 2 to 7 (option B as guidance for hand-gathering only; ruled 2026-11-04):
-- s 26(1) and (2), s 27(1), s 28(2), s 29(1) and s 30(2).  Each is also answered on its own above.
-- The answer is a constructor, not a MAYBE: "the exception applies", "no exception applies", or
-- "it cannot be told" (an input the Act leaves outside its text is not given).
-- src:97 | (2) This Part is subject to Part 3; and in relation to contracts, the
-- src:98 | operation of sections 2 to 4 and 7 is subject to the exceptions made by
-- src:99 | the First Schedule.
@ref s 1(2) (src:97-99)
GIVEN kind IS A `Kind of contract`
      part3 IS A `Part 3 facts`
GIVETH A `Reach of a section`
`s 1(2) whether Part 3 takes sections 2 to 7 out of the case` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `any route is a no`
        THEN `An exception takes the section out of the case`
        IF unknown
        THEN `Whether an exception takes the section out of the case cannot be told`
        OTHERWISE `No exception takes the section out of the case`
    WHERE
        `any route is a no` MEANS
                `is a no` (`s 26(1) the limits imposed by this Act on excluding or restricting liability apply to liability under the contract` kind part3)
             OR `is a no` (`s 26(2) the terms of the contract are subject to a requirement of reasonableness under section 3 or 4` kind part3)
             OR `is a no` (`s 27(1) sections 2 to 7 operate as part of the proper law` part3)
             OR `is a no` (`s 28(2) this Act precludes the person from excluding or restricting liability for loss or damage` part3)
             OR `is a no` (`s 29(1) this Act removes or restricts the effect of, or prevents reliance upon, the contractual provision` part3)
             OR `is a no` (`s 30(2) this Act applies in relation to the contract or the liability for loss or damage` part3)
        -- An input the Act leaves outside its text decides whether an exception applies: the Minister's order (s 28(2)) or section 5 of the Civil Law Act 1909 (s 30(2)).
        unknown MEANS
                (   part3's `the contract is for the carriage by sea of a passenger, or of a passenger and luggage`
                AND `is unknown` (part3's `the Minister's order prescribes this exclusion in these circumstances, to this extent, by this term`))
             OR (   (   part3's `the date the contract was made` LESS THAN (Date 12 11 1993)
                     OR part3's `the date the loss or damage was suffered` LESS THAN (Date 12 11 1993))
                AND `is unknown` (part3's `it was applicable by virtue of section 5 of the Civil Law Act 1909 in force before that date`))
